And we get two valid candidates.
This is exactly the standard layout of an ESP32 flash:

0x0000 - 0x0fff  : unallocated space (0xFF) - this is where the chip's boot header sits
0x1000           : bootloader (the second-stage bootloader)
0x8000           : partition table (the map of partitions in flash)
0x10000          : main application (the code we care about)

The code written should be at the main application, let's work into that.
