Now we want to extract the application but we don't know where it finishes so we have to compute according to the esp layout.
`An ESP32 image consists of: a header + a series of segments (each with its own 8-byte mini-header) + a checksum byte (16-aligned) + 32 bytes of SHA256 hash at the end. To know where the image ends, we take the position of the last segment, add its size, align to 16 (as the format requires), then add the 32 bytes of hash. This way we cut out exactly the application image, without the trailing 0xFF surplus.`
```
